1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:01,700
[Disclaimer:
All depicted events are fictional

2
00:00:01,720 --> 00:00:03,450
and for entertainment purposes only;
viewer discretion is advised]

3
00:00:12,160 --> 00:00:17,440
[Your Third Series]

4
00:00:18,020 --> 00:00:18,800
I thought I'd never

5
00:00:18,820 --> 00:00:21,010
feel this way about anyone again in my life...

6
00:00:21,180 --> 00:00:22,710
but this kid is the exception.

7
00:00:24,050 --> 00:00:25,460
Whenever I'm with this one,

8
00:00:25,460 --> 00:00:26,720
I'm over the moon.

9
00:00:26,720 --> 00:00:27,980
I feel really comfortable.

10
00:00:28,790 --> 00:00:29,620
I want us to be together...

11
00:00:29,650 --> 00:00:30,610
Are you hitting on me?

12
00:00:30,980 --> 00:00:32,450
Yes, just now realizing that?

13
00:00:36,000 --> 00:00:45,680
[Two weeks later]

14
00:01:09,370 --> 00:01:10,340
- Jam.
- Oh!

15
00:01:11,550 --> 00:01:12,580
Mr. Sarm.

16
00:01:22,570 --> 00:01:23,810
What is it?

17
00:01:24,400 --> 00:01:25,170
Nothing.

18
00:01:26,170 --> 00:01:27,010
I'm here to see you.

19
00:01:29,410 --> 00:01:30,610
Why are you here to see me?

20
00:01:31,920 --> 00:01:33,009
♫Why am I here?♫

21
00:01:33,200 --> 00:01:34,700
♫If I didn't love you, I wouldn't be here♫

22
00:01:36,130 --> 00:01:36,860
Confused?

23
00:01:37,220 --> 00:01:38,020
Ever heard of it?

24
00:01:39,340 --> 00:01:40,460
Never heard of the song.

25
00:01:45,000 --> 00:01:46,200
It is probably before my time.

26
00:01:51,500 --> 00:01:53,009
Why are you here, really?

27
00:01:53,600 --> 00:01:55,050
Why do you not go back to your place?

28
00:01:56,690 --> 00:01:57,570
It's you

29
00:01:58,530 --> 00:01:59,410
who is my home.

30
00:02:04,710 --> 00:02:05,850
Can I borrow the chair?

31
00:02:07,320 --> 00:02:08,580
What are you doing?

32
00:02:46,850 --> 00:02:47,590
- Boo!
- Whoa!

33
00:02:49,130 --> 00:02:50,690
Why did you trick me?

34
00:02:51,350 --> 00:02:51,880
Eh?

35
00:02:52,380 --> 00:02:53,850
How did I trick you, exactly?

36
00:02:54,340 --> 00:02:55,579
You were not sleeping.

37
00:02:57,640 --> 00:02:58,780
I was, actually.

38
00:02:59,170 --> 00:03:00,040
Well,

39
00:03:00,040 --> 00:03:01,300
the moment I sat down

40
00:03:01,530 --> 00:03:02,660
and put my head on the table,

41
00:03:02,680 --> 00:03:03,900
I fell right asleep.

42
00:03:04,560 --> 00:03:06,190
Then I woke up because I got hungry.

43
00:03:06,610 --> 00:03:07,810
- Is this for me?
- Hey.

44
00:03:08,100 --> 00:03:08,980
No, it is not yours.

45
00:03:09,260 --> 00:03:10,190
Not yours.

46
00:03:10,210 --> 00:03:10,810
What?

47
00:03:11,110 --> 00:03:12,090
It is yours.

48
00:03:14,630 --> 00:03:15,300
Thank you.

49
00:03:22,450 --> 00:03:23,410
Alright.

50
00:03:23,680 --> 00:03:25,810
Since you made it, I have to serve it to you, too.

51
00:03:48,700 --> 00:03:50,630
Actually, it was great back at the beach.

52
00:03:59,240 --> 00:04:00,440
Which moment?

53
00:04:04,080 --> 00:04:06,970
Was it when you got talked into climbing the coconut tree

54
00:04:07,170 --> 00:04:08,420
and got stuck?

55
00:04:09,140 --> 00:04:09,700
Hey.

56
00:04:09,750 --> 00:04:10,480
Listen.

57
00:04:10,890 --> 00:04:12,330
Can you not rub it in so much?

58
00:04:13,500 --> 00:04:14,660
I get embarrassed too, you know.

59
00:04:14,990 --> 00:04:16,079
It wasn't just me, though.

60
00:04:16,850 --> 00:04:17,700
You

61
00:04:18,130 --> 00:04:20,740
sang a duet with me
and got a perfect score at karaoke, no?

62
00:04:21,170 --> 00:04:22,760
Who else, if not you?

63
00:04:26,470 --> 00:04:27,650
I was there for six whole months,

64
00:04:28,960 --> 00:04:30,380
but if any of it truly meant something...

65
00:04:30,610 --> 00:04:31,810
it was those last two weeks.

66
00:04:38,310 --> 00:04:39,430
How so, may I ask?

67
00:04:47,720 --> 00:04:48,890
It's like...

68
00:04:55,159 --> 00:04:56,200
I met someone...

69
00:04:57,440 --> 00:04:58,790
who made my heart race.

70
00:05:05,720 --> 00:05:06,900
Obviously.

71
00:05:07,340 --> 00:05:09,470
You were being hunted down

72
00:05:09,830 --> 00:05:10,780
and on the run,

73
00:05:12,490 --> 00:05:15,010
so it was only natural for your heart to be racing.

74
00:05:18,800 --> 00:05:19,430
Right?

75
00:05:20,090 --> 00:05:20,700
Mm.

76
00:05:26,310 --> 00:05:26,870
And...

77
00:05:27,570 --> 00:05:29,180
you're not scared of ghosts when you're here alone?

78
00:05:31,330 --> 00:05:32,560
I am not, actually.

79
00:05:35,560 --> 00:05:36,790
I'm a ghost, too, you know?

80
00:05:37,440 --> 00:05:38,440
Are you scared of me?

81
00:05:39,150 --> 00:05:40,200
- Boo!
- Whoa!

82
00:05:44,010 --> 00:05:45,010
Someone like you?

83
00:05:45,040 --> 00:05:47,040
Even a shaman could not handle you.

84
00:05:47,380 --> 00:05:48,430
You...

85
00:05:48,790 --> 00:05:50,420
Despite being this tiny,

86
00:05:50,460 --> 00:05:51,800
you're full of attitude, aren't you?

87
00:05:52,800 --> 00:05:54,370
Even a shaman couldn't handle me,

88
00:05:55,040 --> 00:05:56,120
but...

89
00:05:57,010 --> 00:05:57,760
you...

90
00:05:58,450 --> 00:05:59,220
you can.

91
00:06:05,140 --> 00:06:06,900
When will you promote me to number one?

92
00:06:11,620 --> 00:06:12,220
Hm?

93
00:06:12,650 --> 00:06:13,110
Hm?

94
00:06:13,910 --> 00:06:14,540
Hmm?

95
00:06:18,310 --> 00:06:19,270
Never mind.

96
00:06:21,010 --> 00:06:22,000
Let's just say...

97
00:06:22,800 --> 00:06:24,010
when you feel like it,

98
00:06:25,330 --> 00:06:26,760
give me a kiss on the cheek...

99
00:06:27,010 --> 00:06:28,210
as your answer, then.

100
00:06:28,310 --> 00:06:28,770
Here.

101
00:06:39,670 --> 00:06:40,860
Mm.

102
00:06:42,070 --> 00:06:42,800
Tasty.

103
00:06:43,860 --> 00:06:45,320
How has it been working here?

104
00:06:46,210 --> 00:06:47,140
Is everything okay?

105
00:06:48,610 --> 00:06:50,440
It has been exhausting but quite fun.

106
00:06:51,510 --> 00:06:53,200
At first, I could not sleep well.

107
00:06:54,960 --> 00:06:57,510
Once I got used to the surroundings,

108
00:06:58,450 --> 00:07:00,100
I ended up barely getting any sleep either.

109
00:07:00,610 --> 00:07:02,130
I have been very busy.

110
00:07:04,980 --> 00:07:07,090
You have to visit the weir
with Mr. Wasin tomorrow, right?

111
00:07:08,100 --> 00:07:09,010
Precisely.

112
00:07:10,210 --> 00:07:11,180
Today,

113
00:07:11,300 --> 00:07:12,710
I just got back from the dam.

114
00:07:12,770 --> 00:07:14,050
It was a blast.

115
00:07:14,710 --> 00:07:16,480
It should be the same tomorrow.

116
00:07:16,820 --> 00:07:19,450
The seniors said
they would grill the fish they caught there.

117
00:07:22,800 --> 00:07:23,410
Really?

118
00:07:23,720 --> 00:07:24,220
Listen.

119
00:07:24,770 --> 00:07:26,760
Don't get too caught up in the fun, okay?

120
00:07:27,540 --> 00:07:28,460
It's dangerous here.

121
00:07:28,700 --> 00:07:30,160
Wherever you go,

122
00:07:30,160 --> 00:07:31,810
keep your eyes peeled,

123
00:07:32,000 --> 00:07:32,860
or you might slip.

124
00:07:34,210 --> 00:07:35,600
Behave yourself. Don't be naughty.

125
00:07:35,840 --> 00:07:37,640
You must wear all the necessary safety equipment

126
00:07:38,120 --> 00:07:39,420
and have everything prepared.

127
00:07:39,930 --> 00:07:41,610
I won't be there to look after you,

128
00:07:41,850 --> 00:07:43,050
so take care of yourself,

129
00:07:45,810 --> 00:07:46,580
okay?

130
00:07:47,540 --> 00:07:48,900
Mm.

131
00:07:50,100 --> 00:07:51,650
I understand.

132
00:07:55,090 --> 00:07:56,120
When you get back,

133
00:07:57,010 --> 00:07:58,450
come and see me first.

134
00:08:00,440 --> 00:08:01,700
There's something I want to talk to you about.

135
00:08:05,380 --> 00:08:06,820
What is it?

136
00:08:07,940 --> 00:08:09,710
Can you not just tell me?

137
00:08:14,330 --> 00:08:15,280
Your heart...

138
00:08:15,840 --> 00:08:17,410
Is it ready for the impact?

139
00:08:25,270 --> 00:08:26,420
Mm...

140
00:08:29,290 --> 00:08:29,860
Uh...

141
00:08:29,890 --> 00:08:30,970
Between us,

142
00:08:34,010 --> 00:08:34,780
well...

143
00:08:35,720 --> 00:08:36,610
You...

144
00:08:37,330 --> 00:08:38,169
Little Jam...

145
00:08:41,640 --> 00:08:43,120
My feelings

146
00:08:43,429 --> 00:08:44,680
have changed,

147
00:08:44,700 --> 00:08:46,060
and I don't know when.

148
00:08:47,210 --> 00:08:48,820
They've changed for the better, though.

149
00:08:50,020 --> 00:08:50,600
Like...

150
00:08:53,110 --> 00:08:54,520
I'm not joking here either.

151
00:08:55,960 --> 00:08:57,510
I've been thinking about it over and over.

152
00:08:59,320 --> 00:09:00,440
I've thought this through.

153
00:09:04,630 --> 00:09:05,770
I like you.

154
00:09:07,040 --> 00:09:07,620
Like...

155
00:09:07,910 --> 00:09:09,010
I've really fallen for you.

156
00:09:12,140 --> 00:09:13,020
Actually...

157
00:09:14,000 --> 00:09:15,980
it's more than just "like."

158
00:09:22,640 --> 00:09:24,140
You're quiet because you're shy?

159
00:09:26,790 --> 00:09:27,800
Don't be.

160
00:09:28,820 --> 00:09:30,150
Because I'm shy, too.

161
00:09:34,420 --> 00:09:35,170
What about you?

162
00:09:36,430 --> 00:09:37,290
Do you feel the same?

163
00:09:41,140 --> 00:09:41,770
Oh...

164
00:09:41,980 --> 00:09:42,400
Asleep...

165
00:10:01,320 --> 00:10:06,600
[Your Third Series]

166
00:10:16,800 --> 00:10:20,730
♫Still feeling lonely? Well, you've got me,♫

167
00:10:20,770 --> 00:10:25,210
♫Keeping you busy every day♫

168
00:10:25,930 --> 00:10:29,870
♫I might not be the one you wanted,♫

169
00:10:29,930 --> 00:10:34,630
♫But give it time, you'll love me anyway♫

170
00:10:35,080 --> 00:10:39,610
♫It's your heart, so it's your choice,♫

171
00:10:39,630 --> 00:10:44,070
♫I won't ever stand in your way♫

172
00:10:44,200 --> 00:10:48,460
♫But when they make you blue,♫

173
00:10:48,510 --> 00:10:52,220
♫Can you please let me take care of you?♫

174
00:10:53,190 --> 00:10:57,860
♫I'm here to love you as myself, not as a surrogate♫

175
00:10:57,900 --> 00:11:01,650
♫Let me be your safe space when you need a break♫

176
00:11:01,680 --> 00:11:06,670
♫Who cares if I'm not your first or second?♫

177
00:11:06,750 --> 00:11:11,220
♫At least being your third still counts♫

178
00:11:11,620 --> 00:11:16,170
♫I'm here to love you,
no matter who left you with heartache♫

179
00:11:16,220 --> 00:11:19,880
♫Just let me heal your heart, lending you my aid♫

180
00:11:19,910 --> 00:11:25,020
♫Have faith and believe in love once more♫

181
00:11:25,050 --> 00:11:27,030
♫'Cause good love is your Lucky Third♫

182
00:11:27,060 --> 00:11:30,260
♫Your Third, can it be me, love?♫

183
00:11:30,280 --> 00:11:33,320
[Your Third Series]

184
00:11:35,920 --> 00:11:38,000
[Office]

185
00:11:49,620 --> 00:11:50,840
What is it? What's going on?

186
00:11:51,590 --> 00:11:53,000
I went to the orchard this morning

187
00:11:53,020 --> 00:11:54,970
and saw a young man, around 20 years old.

188
00:11:55,080 --> 00:11:57,020
I believe he trespassed into the orchard last night.

189
00:11:57,040 --> 00:11:59,040
My guess is that he got lost and tired.

190
00:11:59,040 --> 00:12:00,780
Is he an outsider or one of us?

191
00:12:00,780 --> 00:12:01,880
He's probably not one of ours.

192
00:12:02,150 --> 00:12:03,580
The person taking care of him says

193
00:12:03,580 --> 00:12:05,620
all he does is say your name in his sleep.

194
00:12:06,320 --> 00:12:07,440
After some digging around,

195
00:12:07,460 --> 00:12:09,150
I believe he climbed the guardhouse.

196
00:12:13,370 --> 00:12:17,590
Sarm...

197
00:12:44,560 --> 00:12:45,400
Sarm!

198
00:12:45,700 --> 00:12:47,290
I missed you.

199
00:12:48,160 --> 00:12:48,900
Lantao.

200
00:12:49,420 --> 00:12:50,150
Sit down.

201
00:12:50,620 --> 00:12:51,520
Sit down for a minute.

202
00:12:54,280 --> 00:12:56,560
What has gotten into you,
climbing the fence like that?

203
00:12:57,350 --> 00:12:58,420
Why didn't you just come in properly?

204
00:12:59,110 --> 00:13:01,620
Now that's the real Sarm talking.

205
00:13:01,620 --> 00:13:01,990
Huh?

206
00:13:01,990 --> 00:13:03,590
I missed you so much.

207
00:13:05,100 --> 00:13:07,170
Doing it the normal way isn't memorable, Sarm.

208
00:13:07,190 --> 00:13:09,720
I want to leave an unforgettable impression on you.

209
00:13:11,620 --> 00:13:12,310
And how did that go?

210
00:13:12,420 --> 00:13:12,950
Hm?

211
00:13:13,720 --> 00:13:14,720
Was it worth it?

212
00:13:15,860 --> 00:13:17,180
Your legs almost got hurt, didn't they?

213
00:13:18,170 --> 00:13:19,840
It was worth it just to see you.

214
00:13:20,680 --> 00:13:22,280
Does your dad know you came here?

215
00:13:22,720 --> 00:13:24,400
Don't tell me you ran away from him?

216
00:13:24,420 --> 00:13:25,330
He knew,

217
00:13:25,350 --> 00:13:26,830
and he didn't mind.

218
00:13:27,880 --> 00:13:29,750
You left something behind on Ko Pha-ngan,

219
00:13:29,770 --> 00:13:31,290
and I'm here to return it to you.

220
00:13:32,010 --> 00:13:32,600
Left?

221
00:13:33,220 --> 00:13:33,750
Left what?

222
00:13:34,090 --> 00:13:35,960
You left your heart with me back on the island.

223
00:13:37,280 --> 00:13:39,510
You went home without even saying goodbye to me.

224
00:13:39,770 --> 00:13:40,940
And now I'm at fault

225
00:13:40,940 --> 00:13:42,580
for coming to find my own heart?

226
00:13:42,980 --> 00:13:44,040
Did you find it?

227
00:13:44,080 --> 00:13:45,040
I did.

228
00:13:45,110 --> 00:13:46,230
My beating heart

229
00:13:46,440 --> 00:13:48,200
is right in front of me.

230
00:13:49,960 --> 00:13:50,690
What did the doctor say?

231
00:13:50,810 --> 00:13:52,170
The initial examination

232
00:13:52,190 --> 00:13:54,360
found no bruises or wounds.

233
00:13:54,590 --> 00:13:57,360
But the heart is missing a caretaker.

234
00:13:59,230 --> 00:14:00,310
Can you be serious for a moment?

235
00:14:00,470 --> 00:14:00,950
Hm?

236
00:14:01,600 --> 00:14:02,640
Look at me, okay?

237
00:14:03,160 --> 00:14:03,960
I'm not playing.

238
00:14:04,680 --> 00:14:05,430
Fine!

239
00:14:05,940 --> 00:14:08,150
The doctor said I was simply exhausted

240
00:14:08,380 --> 00:14:10,740
and told me to rest up for a bit.

241
00:14:11,000 --> 00:14:12,950
Please, just don't kick me out.

242
00:14:13,240 --> 00:14:15,330
I've already decided that

243
00:14:15,350 --> 00:14:16,300
I'm staying here.

244
00:14:16,320 --> 00:14:17,170
Staying here?

245
00:14:17,200 --> 00:14:18,030
Yes!

246
00:14:18,110 --> 00:14:18,600
Oh?

247
00:14:18,740 --> 00:14:20,820
Please let me work with you.

248
00:14:20,840 --> 00:14:22,420
I can do everything.

249
00:14:22,550 --> 00:14:25,590
You already knew I could climb the guardhouse.

250
00:14:25,790 --> 00:14:27,350
Your dozens of guards

251
00:14:27,590 --> 00:14:29,240
couldn't even catch me.

252
00:14:29,630 --> 00:14:32,180
I'm pretty good at sneaking around, you know.

253
00:14:33,120 --> 00:14:34,020
Lantao.

254
00:14:35,000 --> 00:14:35,850
How about this?

255
00:14:36,170 --> 00:14:37,160
Once you've recovered,

256
00:14:37,450 --> 00:14:38,210
we'll talk about it.

257
00:14:38,800 --> 00:14:40,440
Your hand's so warm, Sarm.

258
00:14:45,860 --> 00:14:46,680
I have to go to work now.

259
00:14:46,700 --> 00:14:47,500
No.

260
00:14:47,520 --> 00:14:48,950
I don't wanna be alone.

261
00:14:49,050 --> 00:14:50,410
Sarm,

262
00:14:50,830 --> 00:14:52,620
please stay with me.

263
00:14:57,820 --> 00:14:58,550
Sarm?!

264
00:15:05,780 --> 00:15:07,450
Why are there two of you?

265
00:15:08,550 --> 00:15:09,830
What do you think?

266
00:15:10,390 --> 00:15:11,290
It's good that you're here.

267
00:15:11,580 --> 00:15:12,430
Take care of him for me.

268
00:15:12,450 --> 00:15:13,670
And don't tease him too much, either.

269
00:15:13,690 --> 00:15:14,470
I'm begging you.

270
00:15:14,700 --> 00:15:15,350
Sure.

271
00:15:15,560 --> 00:15:18,900
Go enjoy paying the price for
abandoning your work for six months.

272
00:15:19,430 --> 00:15:20,150
Also...

273
00:15:20,260 --> 00:15:22,260
Come have dinner at the main house.

274
00:15:22,280 --> 00:15:22,990
Dad's missing you.

275
00:15:23,150 --> 00:15:23,580
Mm.

276
00:15:25,510 --> 00:15:26,380
Please no!

277
00:15:26,500 --> 00:15:28,030
- Sarm!
- Kiddo.

278
00:15:28,860 --> 00:15:30,070
Sarm.

279
00:15:31,400 --> 00:15:32,170
Hey, Lantao!

280
00:15:32,420 --> 00:15:33,220
Why are you so strong?

281
00:15:33,440 --> 00:15:34,070
I have to go now.

282
00:15:34,090 --> 00:15:34,990
Go on.

283
00:15:35,860 --> 00:15:36,590
Little boy.

284
00:15:37,160 --> 00:15:38,150
Have a seat.

285
00:15:39,360 --> 00:15:41,240
Sarm has a ton of work ahead of him.

286
00:15:41,260 --> 00:15:42,650
No, I refuse to listen!

287
00:15:42,670 --> 00:15:43,360
Will you listen to me?

288
00:15:43,360 --> 00:15:43,880
No!

289
00:15:43,890 --> 00:15:45,160
You're a bad boy, aren't you?

290
00:15:45,180 --> 00:15:45,800
Not listening!

291
00:15:45,820 --> 00:15:47,050
What will the bad boy get?

292
00:15:47,070 --> 00:15:47,540
Don't know!

293
00:15:47,560 --> 00:15:48,970
- Here's your flick.
- Ow!

294
00:15:50,710 --> 00:15:51,000
Ah!

295
00:15:51,000 --> 00:15:51,620
Whoa!

296
00:15:51,900 --> 00:15:53,460
Gosh, Song, you jerk!

297
00:15:53,750 --> 00:15:55,200
I told you not to tease him.

298
00:16:10,230 --> 00:16:11,060
Who's that kid?

299
00:16:11,250 --> 00:16:12,760
Oh, that's Mr. Jam.

300
00:16:12,780 --> 00:16:14,150
He's Mr. Sib's man.

301
00:16:14,840 --> 00:16:15,800
Mr. Sib's man?

302
00:16:15,820 --> 00:16:16,450
Correct.

303
00:16:16,730 --> 00:16:18,580
Is he having a secret affair?

304
00:16:19,470 --> 00:16:20,440
It's not like that.

305
00:16:20,460 --> 00:16:21,590
Uh, well...

306
00:16:21,610 --> 00:16:24,280
Mr. Jam is his assistant.

307
00:16:25,220 --> 00:16:26,010
His assistant?

308
00:16:26,030 --> 00:16:27,200
Yes, his assistant.

309
00:16:31,880 --> 00:16:33,510
You can go back alone, right?

310
00:16:34,190 --> 00:16:35,750
A piece of cake, Wasin.

311
00:16:35,880 --> 00:16:36,620
Very well.

312
00:16:36,640 --> 00:16:38,800
Let's have a meal with the workers, then.

313
00:16:39,200 --> 00:16:39,850
Right.

314
00:16:40,000 --> 00:16:40,550
Let's go.

315
00:16:40,860 --> 00:16:41,250
- Hey!
- Whoa!

316
00:16:41,270 --> 00:16:42,590
- Jam! Be careful!
- Mr. Jam!

317
00:16:43,380 --> 00:16:44,460
Mind your legs.

318
00:16:45,880 --> 00:16:47,000
Are you alright, Mr. Jam?

319
00:16:48,510 --> 00:16:48,980
Where does it hurt?

320
00:16:49,110 --> 00:16:50,460
My foot hurts.

321
00:16:51,160 --> 00:16:53,370
We need to take him to the medical center, Mr. Thee.

322
00:16:53,660 --> 00:16:54,660
I'll take him there.

323
00:17:01,060 --> 00:17:03,290
You're new here, so I guess you don't know who I am.

324
00:17:03,920 --> 00:17:05,319
Allow me to introduce myself.

325
00:17:06,130 --> 00:17:06,940
I'm Thee,

326
00:17:07,560 --> 00:17:08,869
a caretaker here.

327
00:17:10,970 --> 00:17:12,160
I am Jam...

328
00:17:12,700 --> 00:17:13,810
Jiranat,

329
00:17:14,349 --> 00:17:15,520
and I am Mr. Sib's assistant.

330
00:17:25,210 --> 00:17:27,170
Once you get home,
try not to use your hand too much,

331
00:17:27,190 --> 00:17:28,550
or it might swell and ache.

332
00:17:29,750 --> 00:17:30,360
Right.

333
00:17:31,350 --> 00:17:32,150
Jam.

334
00:17:32,550 --> 00:17:33,870
Excuse me for a moment.

335
00:17:35,210 --> 00:17:35,950
Okay.

336
00:17:36,630 --> 00:17:38,450
Which worker's quarters are you staying in, Jam?

337
00:17:38,470 --> 00:17:40,430
I'll call a ride to take you there.

338
00:17:40,550 --> 00:17:42,370
And once you're there,

339
00:17:42,390 --> 00:17:43,750
don't forget to take the medicine.

340
00:17:44,470 --> 00:17:45,350
Understood.

341
00:17:45,540 --> 00:17:47,730
I'll go and prescribe the medicine for you.

342
00:17:47,750 --> 00:17:48,950
Wait a moment, okay?

343
00:17:49,560 --> 00:17:50,600
- Okay.
- Alright.

344
00:17:57,350 --> 00:17:58,630
- Hey Little Jam!
- Whoa, Mr. Sarm?!

345
00:17:58,650 --> 00:17:59,340
- Little Jam!
- How did you get here?

346
00:17:59,360 --> 00:18:00,080
Ow...

347
00:18:00,100 --> 00:18:00,950
Ow! Hey!

348
00:18:03,660 --> 00:18:04,680
Let go of me first.

349
00:18:04,700 --> 00:18:05,380
Jam.

350
00:18:05,940 --> 00:18:06,400
Aww!

351
00:18:06,420 --> 00:18:07,280
Are you hurt?

352
00:18:07,660 --> 00:18:08,570
Gosh...

353
00:18:08,950 --> 00:18:09,900
Little Jam!

354
00:18:10,810 --> 00:18:12,310
I've heard from the workers

355
00:18:12,310 --> 00:18:14,130
that you slipped and fell over,

356
00:18:14,150 --> 00:18:14,980
broke all your limbs,

357
00:18:15,000 --> 00:18:15,940
and split your head open!

358
00:18:18,890 --> 00:18:20,650
- You...
- Does it hurt a lot?

359
00:18:22,970 --> 00:18:24,030
Don't worry, though.

360
00:18:24,050 --> 00:18:24,970
That stream,

361
00:18:25,050 --> 00:18:26,020
it's getting buried.

362
00:18:26,340 --> 00:18:28,310
You got hurt by it, so it deserves to disappear.

363
00:18:30,950 --> 00:18:32,330
Do not overreact.

364
00:18:32,550 --> 00:18:34,080
I am fine, actually.

365
00:18:34,330 --> 00:18:35,010
Gosh...

366
00:18:35,030 --> 00:18:36,950
What did you do to slip?

367
00:18:38,950 --> 00:18:40,540
I was simply being careless.

368
00:18:40,830 --> 00:18:41,880
Oh, Little Jam...

369
00:18:43,750 --> 00:18:44,380
Come on.

370
00:18:44,940 --> 00:18:45,690
Let's go home.

371
00:18:46,000 --> 00:18:46,870
I'm here to pick you up.

372
00:18:47,430 --> 00:18:48,080
Mm.

373
00:18:48,780 --> 00:18:49,350
Let's go.

374
00:18:49,370 --> 00:18:50,010
Here.

375
00:18:50,680 --> 00:18:51,350
Take it slow.

376
00:18:51,370 --> 00:18:52,060
Oh, oh.

377
00:18:53,310 --> 00:18:54,090
Oh, be careful.

378
00:18:55,150 --> 00:18:55,830
Here, here.

379
00:18:58,140 --> 00:18:59,020
Ow...

380
00:18:59,750 --> 00:19:01,180
- Take it slow, okay?
- Right.

381
00:19:02,720 --> 00:19:03,540
Slowly.

382
00:19:03,560 --> 00:19:04,360
Gently.

383
00:19:04,380 --> 00:19:04,810
Oh.

384
00:19:04,830 --> 00:19:05,750
Slowly.

385
00:19:06,090 --> 00:19:06,950
Gently now.

386
00:19:08,660 --> 00:19:10,270
Are you okay? Take it slow.

387
00:19:20,360 --> 00:19:21,870
Where did the patient in this bed go?

388
00:19:22,430 --> 00:19:23,350
It seems...

389
00:19:23,370 --> 00:19:24,950
Jam has already gone home.

390
00:19:26,150 --> 00:19:27,140
He already went home?

391
00:19:27,350 --> 00:19:27,850
Yes.

392
00:19:45,590 --> 00:19:47,370
This is not the way back to my worker's quarters.

393
00:19:52,510 --> 00:19:54,430
Who says you have to go back and live alone?

394
00:19:55,050 --> 00:19:55,960
You're staying with me.

395
00:19:57,820 --> 00:19:59,320
But I want to go back to my quarters.

396
00:19:59,730 --> 00:20:00,370
Listen.

397
00:20:02,430 --> 00:20:04,190
Your hand and leg hurt this much.

398
00:20:04,910 --> 00:20:06,160
How can you go back to living alone?

399
00:20:06,750 --> 00:20:07,280
But...

400
00:20:07,280 --> 00:20:08,010
How about this?

401
00:20:08,700 --> 00:20:09,920
It's your choice:

402
00:20:10,900 --> 00:20:12,710
me living with you,

403
00:20:13,420 --> 00:20:14,560
or you living with me.

404
00:20:14,760 --> 00:20:15,350
Decide.

405
00:20:15,720 --> 00:20:16,740
Why are you threatening me?

406
00:20:16,740 --> 00:20:17,530
Mm.

407
00:20:18,490 --> 00:20:19,720
Don't change the topic.

408
00:20:19,970 --> 00:20:20,880
What will it be?

409
00:20:27,440 --> 00:20:28,530
You're taking forever here.

410
00:20:28,550 --> 00:20:29,750
The decision is mine, then.

411
00:20:29,770 --> 00:20:30,600
You're staying with me.

412
00:20:33,910 --> 00:20:34,860
Fine, I guess.

413
00:20:44,880 --> 00:20:45,700
Now then,

414
00:20:46,120 --> 00:20:47,620
where are my lovely children?

415
00:20:47,900 --> 00:20:50,260
Mr. Song declines the dinner invitation,

416
00:20:50,400 --> 00:20:51,870
saying he's on a diet.

417
00:20:52,100 --> 00:20:54,740
As for Mr. Sarm, he recently informed us that

418
00:20:54,760 --> 00:20:56,940
he has a life-or-death matter to attend to.

419
00:20:57,150 --> 00:20:59,320
So he probably won't be joining dinner either.

420
00:21:01,680 --> 00:21:03,210
Can't they all just give me a break?

421
00:21:03,690 --> 00:21:04,780
So this means...

422
00:21:05,160 --> 00:21:06,770
I have to sit here and eat all alone,

423
00:21:06,790 --> 00:21:07,550
hm?

424
00:21:08,030 --> 00:21:09,350
From the looks of it,

425
00:21:09,540 --> 00:21:11,220
it appears so, unfortunately.

426
00:21:13,220 --> 00:21:15,540
The children are starting to keep secrets

427
00:21:15,560 --> 00:21:17,560
and act all suspicious.

428
00:21:17,580 --> 00:21:20,330
They're just like their father.

429
00:21:20,350 --> 00:21:21,060
Hey.

430
00:21:21,350 --> 00:21:21,850
Yes?

431
00:21:21,870 --> 00:21:23,150
Are you talking to a ghost or something?

432
00:21:23,430 --> 00:21:24,560
I can hear

433
00:21:24,580 --> 00:21:25,460
your intrusive thoughts!

434
00:21:25,480 --> 00:21:27,130
Nothing.

435
00:21:27,350 --> 00:21:28,080
By the way...

436
00:21:28,650 --> 00:21:30,030
did Sarm tell you where he's off to?

437
00:21:30,990 --> 00:21:32,720
The reason he gave me was that

438
00:21:32,740 --> 00:21:34,230
he had to take care of Mr. Jam

439
00:21:34,250 --> 00:21:36,350
- after his accident.
- Mm, mm.

440
00:21:37,640 --> 00:21:38,400
Sounds familiar.

441
00:21:38,420 --> 00:21:40,200
I feel like I've heard that name before.

442
00:21:40,550 --> 00:21:41,590
Oh.

443
00:21:41,990 --> 00:21:42,600
Well...

444
00:21:42,700 --> 00:21:45,940
He's the one who brought Mr. Sarm back from the island.

445
00:21:46,440 --> 00:21:47,550
Sib's man?

446
00:21:48,300 --> 00:21:48,980
Then...

447
00:21:49,190 --> 00:21:51,330
What does his accident have to do with Sarm,

448
00:21:51,350 --> 00:21:51,930
huh?

449
00:21:51,950 --> 00:21:53,770
I'm afraid I don't know about that either.

450
00:21:55,500 --> 00:21:56,150
Just go.

451
00:21:58,460 --> 00:22:00,790
- Play me ten songs or so.
- Right away.

452
00:22:00,810 --> 00:22:02,860
Until my migraine is gone.

453
00:22:09,350 --> 00:22:10,550
Mr. Sarm,

454
00:22:11,210 --> 00:22:13,800
I forgot my shirt and towel.

455
00:22:14,060 --> 00:22:16,150
Can you grab them for me?

456
00:22:24,950 --> 00:22:26,150
Mr. Sarm?

457
00:22:37,100 --> 00:22:38,590
Sarm...

458
00:22:38,680 --> 00:22:39,350
Yes?

459
00:22:41,420 --> 00:22:44,680
Can you grab me my shirt and towel, please?

460
00:22:45,350 --> 00:22:47,280
I forgot to bring them with me.

461
00:22:47,300 --> 00:22:48,140
Mm...

462
00:22:48,160 --> 00:22:48,950
You...

463
00:22:49,420 --> 00:22:50,150
Little Jam.

464
00:22:50,820 --> 00:22:51,610
Who...

465
00:22:52,120 --> 00:22:53,080
did you ask to grab the stuff for you?

466
00:22:56,490 --> 00:22:58,480
Sarm, of course.

467
00:22:59,550 --> 00:23:01,720
I asked you to grab them for me, Sarm.

468
00:23:03,560 --> 00:23:04,290
Who?

469
00:23:06,280 --> 00:23:07,610
Sarm, obviously.

470
00:23:08,020 --> 00:23:09,350
No problem.

471
00:23:15,190 --> 00:23:16,340
Mm...

472
00:23:17,660 --> 00:23:18,580
Keep calling me that.

473
00:23:19,930 --> 00:23:20,790
You'll get used to it.

474
00:23:24,810 --> 00:23:25,790
Wash up properly, alright?

475
00:23:33,940 --> 00:23:35,380
Come to think of it...

476
00:23:35,750 --> 00:23:38,150
Mr. Sarm does know how to make sense when he talks.

477
00:23:38,810 --> 00:23:40,170
I think...

478
00:23:40,550 --> 00:23:43,550
I am starting to figure him out.

479
00:24:02,170 --> 00:24:03,370
Cock-a-doodle-doo!

480
00:24:03,750 --> 00:24:04,400
Wake up!

481
00:24:04,720 --> 00:24:05,100
Get up!

482
00:24:05,120 --> 00:24:05,740
Whoa!

483
00:24:07,240 --> 00:24:07,770
So?

484
00:24:08,400 --> 00:24:09,860
You told me to wake you up early, didn't you?

485
00:24:10,120 --> 00:24:10,550
Hm?

486
00:24:11,200 --> 00:24:12,230
It's getting late.

487
00:24:14,990 --> 00:24:16,180
Oh...

488
00:24:16,550 --> 00:24:17,750
Slept soundly, huh?

489
00:24:19,990 --> 00:24:20,960
Why do you want to get up so early?

490
00:24:21,200 --> 00:24:22,260
Where are you going?

491
00:24:22,910 --> 00:24:23,480
Hm?

492
00:24:24,190 --> 00:24:24,950
Where?

493
00:24:26,060 --> 00:24:27,560
To work, obviously.

494
00:24:28,390 --> 00:24:30,580
I have so many things to deal with.

495
00:24:30,600 --> 00:24:31,340
Take a day off.

496
00:24:31,980 --> 00:24:33,350
You're not fully recovered.

497
00:24:33,480 --> 00:24:34,980
How could I?

498
00:24:35,340 --> 00:24:36,590
You would not understand, Mr. Sarm.

499
00:24:36,800 --> 00:24:37,910
"Mr. Sarm" again.

500
00:24:39,470 --> 00:24:42,180
Well, I want to call you "Mr. Sarm."

501
00:24:44,010 --> 00:24:44,780
Fine.

502
00:24:45,260 --> 00:24:46,390
If that's what you want to call me,

503
00:24:47,660 --> 00:24:49,520
then replace "a-r-m" with "p-o-u-s-e" instead.

504
00:24:50,750 --> 00:24:51,830
What is it,

505
00:24:51,850 --> 00:24:53,450
Mr. S-pouse?

506
00:24:53,470 --> 00:24:54,720
- Yes, what is it, dear?
- Hey.

507
00:24:55,800 --> 00:24:56,750
I did not call you that.

508
00:24:57,160 --> 00:24:58,550
Keep calling me that. You'll get used to it.

509
00:24:59,220 --> 00:25:00,150
Mr. Spouse.

510
00:25:00,340 --> 00:25:01,760
Mr. Spouse, Mr. Spouse.

511
00:25:02,750 --> 00:25:03,670
Mr. Sarm.

512
00:25:03,690 --> 00:25:04,570
Mr. Sarm again?

513
00:25:05,220 --> 00:25:06,040
It's "Mr. Spouse."

514
00:25:06,300 --> 00:25:07,160
Mr. Spouse.

515
00:25:07,470 --> 00:25:08,150
Mr. Spouse.

516
00:25:08,630 --> 00:25:10,090
Mr. Spouse, Mr. Spouse.

517
00:25:10,390 --> 00:25:11,160
Mr. Spouse.

518
00:25:11,170 --> 00:25:12,670
Are you not working today?

519
00:25:12,840 --> 00:25:14,150
I am, but how can I?

520
00:25:14,970 --> 00:25:16,550
I'm waiting to get the kitten's wounds cleaned.

521
00:25:18,440 --> 00:25:19,520
I am not a cat.

522
00:25:19,830 --> 00:25:20,730
Oh, right.

523
00:25:21,390 --> 00:25:22,300
You're not a cat.

524
00:25:23,080 --> 00:25:24,200
With such ferocity,

525
00:25:24,520 --> 00:25:25,680
you're basically a mighty tiger.

526
00:25:30,200 --> 00:25:31,580
With a hint of a wild bull.

527
00:25:34,090 --> 00:25:35,160
Mr. Sarm!

528
00:25:41,210 --> 00:25:42,140
Just kidding.

529
00:25:42,640 --> 00:25:43,610
Don't get mad, please.

530
00:25:48,110 --> 00:25:49,220
Okay, I'll stop.

531
00:25:49,430 --> 00:25:49,950
Hey.

532
00:25:50,830 --> 00:25:52,100
Go take a shower already

533
00:25:52,120 --> 00:25:53,490
so you can have breakfast.

534
00:25:54,580 --> 00:25:55,430
For today's breakfast...

535
00:25:57,150 --> 00:25:58,300
I'm the one doing the cooking.

536
00:26:00,180 --> 00:26:00,710
Come on.

537
00:26:02,320 --> 00:26:03,050
Right.

538
00:26:04,740 --> 00:26:05,300
Ow...

539
00:26:09,710 --> 00:26:10,550
Need a lift?

540
00:26:14,270 --> 00:26:15,760
It is okay.

541
00:26:16,490 --> 00:26:18,760
Just your hand will do.

542
00:26:19,270 --> 00:26:20,150
Sure thing.

543
00:26:20,970 --> 00:26:22,090
My left hand,

544
00:26:23,450 --> 00:26:24,760
or my right hand?

545
00:26:29,640 --> 00:26:30,320
My right hand?

546
00:26:31,310 --> 00:26:32,180
Oh, oh, oh.

547
00:26:33,050 --> 00:26:33,680
Better put it down.

548
00:26:33,790 --> 00:26:34,580
Just kidding.

549
00:26:35,070 --> 00:26:35,780
A hand, then.

550
00:26:40,010 --> 00:26:41,090
Oh, oh.

551
00:26:41,090 --> 00:26:42,520
Are you sure you can walk?

552
00:26:42,980 --> 00:26:43,770
Yes.

553
00:26:43,800 --> 00:26:44,960
Let's go.

554
00:26:44,980 --> 00:26:46,400
Oh, here, here.

555
00:26:49,370 --> 00:26:50,540
It's like you've got a broken leg.

556
00:26:54,490 --> 00:26:56,210
Today's breakfast is

557
00:26:57,050 --> 00:26:58,580
shiitake mushroom porridge.

558
00:27:00,010 --> 00:27:00,980
Smells wonderful.

559
00:27:01,450 --> 00:27:04,690
Served with giant deep-fried crab meat rolls...

560
00:27:04,720 --> 00:27:05,430
Ha!

561
00:27:05,770 --> 00:27:08,120
Along with steamed enoki mushrooms in soy sauce.

562
00:27:08,180 --> 00:27:09,410
And the most important dish of all...

563
00:27:09,440 --> 00:27:14,160
stir-fried flower crab with black pepper...

564
00:27:14,180 --> 00:27:16,090
All prepared by...

565
00:27:17,310 --> 00:27:18,440
yours truly.

566
00:27:21,220 --> 00:27:22,270
Please enjoy.

567
00:27:23,170 --> 00:27:24,980
Never knew you could cook.

568
00:27:25,500 --> 00:27:26,650
They're all delicious.

569
00:27:26,680 --> 00:27:27,530
Try them.

570
00:27:27,550 --> 00:27:28,920
Which one is the tastiest?

571
00:27:29,610 --> 00:27:30,980
The tastiest one...

572
00:27:32,860 --> 00:27:34,140
is me, of course.

573
00:27:34,200 --> 00:27:35,140
I'm the tastiest.

574
00:27:50,630 --> 00:27:51,610
Mm.

575
00:27:52,740 --> 00:27:53,600
It really does taste good.

576
00:27:53,630 --> 00:27:54,980
Ha-ha, I knew it.

577
00:27:54,980 --> 00:27:56,810
If you enjoy the food, you have to come and see me

578
00:27:56,840 --> 00:27:58,260
so you can enjoy it more often.

579
00:27:59,390 --> 00:28:00,760
You talk as if you are not busy.

580
00:28:01,450 --> 00:28:04,310
I see you come home
exhausted every day, all wet and dirty.

581
00:28:06,310 --> 00:28:07,590
For you, Little Jam,

582
00:28:07,910 --> 00:28:10,090
you're always my first priority.

583
00:28:12,850 --> 00:28:14,810
Not only can I cook,

584
00:28:15,230 --> 00:28:16,650
but I can do it all,

585
00:28:16,680 --> 00:28:17,700
fixing electrical faults

586
00:28:18,350 --> 00:28:19,600
or even burst water pipes.

587
00:28:19,870 --> 00:28:20,350
Oh...

588
00:28:20,590 --> 00:28:21,020
Oh.

589
00:28:21,270 --> 00:28:21,820
Oh!

590
00:28:22,040 --> 00:28:22,990
You're sore?

591
00:28:23,410 --> 00:28:25,550
I can give you a massage.

592
00:28:25,970 --> 00:28:26,960
If you're stressed out,

593
00:28:27,150 --> 00:28:28,340
I can crack some jokes for you.

594
00:28:28,370 --> 00:28:29,410
Ha-ha!

595
00:28:29,870 --> 00:28:31,560
Or if you want to go somewhere,

596
00:28:31,600 --> 00:28:32,950
even on a long trip,

597
00:28:32,980 --> 00:28:35,180
I can take you there

598
00:28:35,570 --> 00:28:38,020
no matter how far it is.

599
00:28:38,920 --> 00:28:40,050
Or if you want to

600
00:28:40,090 --> 00:28:41,510
rest on my shoulder,

601
00:28:41,540 --> 00:28:42,580
be my guest.

602
00:28:42,600 --> 00:28:44,370
If you want a warm hug,

603
00:28:44,720 --> 00:28:46,570
I'm happy to give you one.

604
00:28:47,070 --> 00:28:48,320
I take better care of you

605
00:28:48,350 --> 00:28:49,500
than any insurance company could.

606
00:28:50,490 --> 00:28:52,320
I can give you advice on anything.

607
00:28:52,830 --> 00:28:54,770
I never slack on external affairs,

608
00:28:55,150 --> 00:28:56,870
nor do I ease up on internal matters.

609
00:28:57,610 --> 00:29:00,260
Because this is me, Sarm. Who else could it be?

610
00:29:01,910 --> 00:29:02,630
Happy.

611
00:29:04,950 --> 00:29:05,590
Yes?

612
00:29:10,850 --> 00:29:11,760
I flirted,

613
00:29:11,780 --> 00:29:13,140
threw countless hints,

614
00:29:13,160 --> 00:29:14,380
and served myself on a silver platter,

615
00:29:15,070 --> 00:29:16,840
yet he still didn't get it.

616
00:29:17,910 --> 00:29:19,370
Or do I have to spell it out

617
00:29:19,980 --> 00:29:21,380
and say, "I love you, kiddo"?!

618
00:29:21,910 --> 00:29:22,380
Oh...

619
00:29:23,100 --> 00:29:24,150
I've become shy.

620
00:29:26,070 --> 00:29:28,580
All I can do is act playful,

621
00:29:29,070 --> 00:29:30,760
so he thinks I'm just fooling around.

622
00:29:36,170 --> 00:29:38,040
Though we're close,

623
00:29:38,950 --> 00:29:41,620
it feels like there's a wall between us,

624
00:29:42,310 --> 00:29:43,920
keeping us far apart.

625
00:29:44,860 --> 00:29:46,360
This injury

626
00:29:46,980 --> 00:29:48,820
reminds me of our time on the island.

627
00:29:49,880 --> 00:29:53,160
Back then, he never left me behind,

628
00:29:55,160 --> 00:29:57,870
even though he could have just tossed me into the ocean.

629
00:30:00,980 --> 00:30:02,740
Part of me feels delighted,

630
00:30:03,430 --> 00:30:05,320
yet the other part tells me to stay away

631
00:30:05,760 --> 00:30:08,160
and not fall for him any further.

632
00:30:09,380 --> 00:30:11,430
Mr. Sarm loves making me feel things,

633
00:30:12,310 --> 00:30:13,620
but I won't budge.

634
00:30:15,320 --> 00:30:16,940
He loves playing with my heart,

635
00:30:17,660 --> 00:30:19,330
but I won't bite.

636
00:30:28,550 --> 00:30:29,600
Whatever it might be,

637
00:30:29,630 --> 00:30:31,040
you must stay at my place.

638
00:30:31,390 --> 00:30:33,800
I am not that injured.

639
00:30:35,000 --> 00:30:36,370
I can take care of myself.

640
00:30:36,570 --> 00:30:38,180
I accept no objections.

641
00:30:38,700 --> 00:30:39,610
No.

642
00:30:40,310 --> 00:30:42,280
I cannot sleep well at your place.

643
00:30:51,670 --> 00:30:53,310
Looking all bitter.

644
00:30:54,900 --> 00:30:56,810
Am I really not allowed to disagree?

645
00:30:57,140 --> 00:30:58,580
I did not do anything.

646
00:31:00,660 --> 00:31:02,610
What do I have to do for you to be okay?

647
00:31:05,780 --> 00:31:07,580
I want to hug Mr. Croc to sleep.

648
00:31:10,020 --> 00:31:10,760
Gosh...

649
00:31:11,310 --> 00:31:12,150
Okay.

650
00:31:13,250 --> 00:31:15,030
You can bring him to my place.

651
00:31:32,590 --> 00:31:33,380
How's it going, Ning-nong?

652
00:31:33,480 --> 00:31:34,550
Hello, Sarm.

653
00:31:34,580 --> 00:31:35,380
Hello.

654
00:31:36,600 --> 00:31:38,180
Oh hey, what's up?

655
00:31:38,200 --> 00:31:39,230
Isn't this your day off?

656
00:31:39,800 --> 00:31:41,100
How can I rest?

657
00:31:41,310 --> 00:31:42,610
I'm worried about them.

658
00:31:43,510 --> 00:31:44,070
Right.

659
00:31:44,980 --> 00:31:46,830
This one's highly sought after.

660
00:31:46,850 --> 00:31:48,960
Oh. Just like its father.

661
00:31:50,620 --> 00:31:52,050
So many people want to get a hold of it,

662
00:31:52,170 --> 00:31:53,360
but you don't want to let it go?

663
00:31:53,640 --> 00:31:54,930
Oh, the horse stays with me.

664
00:31:55,740 --> 00:31:57,350
But the offers are extremely high.

665
00:31:57,380 --> 00:31:58,430
They're willing to fight for it.

666
00:31:59,390 --> 00:32:00,420
Money can't buy me.

667
00:32:00,610 --> 00:32:01,590
Whoa...

668
00:32:02,570 --> 00:32:04,590
I really respect what you stand for.

669
00:32:05,950 --> 00:32:07,010
If it's below what I ask, that is.

670
00:32:07,320 --> 00:32:08,360
Ow...

671
00:32:11,420 --> 00:32:13,550
You seem to really love these horses, Sarm.

672
00:32:14,700 --> 00:32:16,260
I, too,

673
00:32:16,580 --> 00:32:18,310
want to have a horse of my own.

674
00:32:18,780 --> 00:32:19,780
I do, of course.

675
00:32:19,980 --> 00:32:21,330
I've been raising them since they were little.

676
00:32:23,400 --> 00:32:24,190
By the way,

677
00:32:24,730 --> 00:32:25,980
you're going to the orange farm?

678
00:32:26,150 --> 00:32:26,820
Yes.

679
00:32:26,850 --> 00:32:28,180
Can I go there with you?

680
00:32:28,530 --> 00:32:29,620
Hop on, then. Come on.

681
00:32:34,420 --> 00:32:35,390
Jam.

682
00:32:39,310 --> 00:32:41,200
- Hello, Doctor Song.
- Hi.

683
00:32:42,450 --> 00:32:44,180
It's been a long while, hasn't it?

684
00:32:44,250 --> 00:32:45,560
What happened to you?

685
00:32:45,670 --> 00:32:47,110
A minor accident.

686
00:32:47,780 --> 00:32:50,010
Yesterday, I went to a weir with Wasin,

687
00:32:50,180 --> 00:32:52,420
but I slipped on the way back.

688
00:32:52,440 --> 00:32:53,270
Aww...

689
00:32:53,640 --> 00:32:55,420
I guess it's a blessing in disguise, isn't it, Jam?

690
00:32:55,850 --> 00:32:57,210
Why did Sarm send you

691
00:32:57,240 --> 00:32:59,060
to be with those men?

692
00:32:59,080 --> 00:33:00,020
Did you get messed with?

693
00:33:00,400 --> 00:33:01,760
Wasin did not do anything to me.

694
00:33:02,180 --> 00:33:03,850
They were all so kind.

695
00:33:04,550 --> 00:33:05,180
No...

696
00:33:05,210 --> 00:33:08,210
I mean, was Sarm messing with you

697
00:33:08,310 --> 00:33:09,860
by making you do a task like that?

698
00:33:10,440 --> 00:33:11,620
I do not think so.

699
00:33:12,140 --> 00:33:14,750
I have to work with every department either way.

700
00:33:14,900 --> 00:33:16,760
Working with Wasin was a lot of fun.

701
00:33:16,980 --> 00:33:18,610
I got to handle all sorts of fun tasks.

702
00:33:19,720 --> 00:33:21,130
Hang in there, Jam.

703
00:33:21,460 --> 00:33:22,960
Come on, shall I order you some dessert?

704
00:33:23,390 --> 00:33:25,430
The harder the work, the more energy you'll need, right?

705
00:33:26,820 --> 00:33:28,820
Don't push yourself too much, okay?

706
00:33:29,060 --> 00:33:30,500
You'll wear yourself out.

707
00:33:31,110 --> 00:33:32,180
Thank you,

708
00:33:33,380 --> 00:33:34,380
but I am still good to go.

709
00:33:34,910 --> 00:33:35,750
"Jiranat"

710
00:33:36,360 --> 00:33:37,810
means "One who cannot afford to lose."

711
00:33:38,790 --> 00:33:41,010
Work isn't everything in life.

712
00:33:41,320 --> 00:33:43,390
It won't do you any good if you ruin your health.

713
00:33:43,870 --> 00:33:44,850
After...

714
00:33:45,070 --> 00:33:46,580
you're done with dessert,

715
00:33:46,770 --> 00:33:48,780
shall we ride around the farm on horseback

716
00:33:49,420 --> 00:33:50,450
to unwind for a bit?

717
00:33:50,860 --> 00:33:51,730
I would love to.

718
00:33:52,160 --> 00:33:53,580
That's more like it.

719
00:33:56,730 --> 00:33:57,230
Alright.

720
00:33:57,260 --> 00:33:57,990
What do you think?

721
00:33:58,150 --> 00:33:59,250
Are you starting to like it here?

722
00:34:01,860 --> 00:34:03,150
I told you, it's peaceful here.

723
00:34:03,380 --> 00:34:04,050
Everyone loves it.

724
00:34:04,440 --> 00:34:05,050
- Whoa!
- Whoa!

725
00:34:05,640 --> 00:34:06,430
Are you okay, Ning-nong?

726
00:34:06,460 --> 00:34:07,250
Sarm.

727
00:34:07,270 --> 00:34:07,910
Oh, Song.

728
00:34:07,920 --> 00:34:09,380
Perfect timing. Take care of him for me.

729
00:34:10,909 --> 00:34:12,260
What are you doing here?

730
00:34:12,620 --> 00:34:13,550
What are you all doing here?

731
00:34:13,880 --> 00:34:14,380
Huh?!

732
00:34:14,760 --> 00:34:15,750
Why are you here?!

733
00:34:16,889 --> 00:34:17,620
Hello?

734
00:34:17,650 --> 00:34:18,980
No one's going to answer my question?

735
00:34:19,040 --> 00:34:19,550
Hey!

736
00:34:19,739 --> 00:34:20,679
There are so many of you here.

737
00:34:20,860 --> 00:34:21,380
What is it?

738
00:34:21,690 --> 00:34:22,739
What are you doing here?

739
00:34:22,770 --> 00:34:24,060
Is my question that difficult?

740
00:34:24,060 --> 00:34:25,750
It's not like I'm asking an Olympiad-level question.

741
00:34:25,750 --> 00:34:26,550
It's not!

742
00:34:26,570 --> 00:34:27,400
It's dead simple!

743
00:34:27,500 --> 00:34:28,840
What are you doing?!

744
00:34:28,860 --> 00:34:29,400
Huh?!

745
00:34:29,420 --> 00:34:32,500
What would you do if our visitors got scared of you?

746
00:34:33,380 --> 00:34:33,770
What the hell?

747
00:34:33,790 --> 00:34:35,190
Why is no one answering me?!

748
00:34:41,219 --> 00:34:42,920
Little Jam is still injured.

749
00:34:43,280 --> 00:34:44,560
I already told him to take a rest.

750
00:34:45,409 --> 00:34:47,540
I should scold him

751
00:34:47,560 --> 00:34:49,620
for being out and about like this.

752
00:34:50,150 --> 00:34:50,900
Gosh, I'm passing out...

753
00:34:50,920 --> 00:34:52,400
- Ah!
- Eek!

754
00:34:53,380 --> 00:34:54,030
Sarm!

755
00:34:54,060 --> 00:34:54,980
Mr. Sarm!

756
00:34:55,030 --> 00:34:56,469
Fucking Sarm!

757
00:34:59,120 --> 00:34:59,890
What should we do?

758
00:35:00,700 --> 00:35:01,460
I guess we have to

759
00:35:02,180 --> 00:35:02,930
give him CPR.

760
00:35:03,240 --> 00:35:04,020
Three...

761
00:35:04,460 --> 00:35:05,430
two...

762
00:35:05,460 --> 00:35:06,170
one...

763
00:35:07,320 --> 00:35:08,180
- Ow!
- Ouch!

764
00:35:11,160 --> 00:35:12,160
Ning-nong, you do it.

765
00:35:12,330 --> 00:35:13,490
But I'm a horse doctor.

766
00:35:13,530 --> 00:35:14,860
Song, you treat people.

767
00:35:14,890 --> 00:35:16,510
But I'm an aesthetic doctor.

768
00:35:16,530 --> 00:35:17,420
Jam.

769
00:35:17,450 --> 00:35:18,960
I am an assistant secretary.

770
00:35:18,980 --> 00:35:20,180
- Please help Sarm.
- Please, Jam.

771
00:35:20,500 --> 00:35:21,870
I really cannot.

772
00:35:22,170 --> 00:35:22,900
Song.

773
00:35:23,180 --> 00:35:24,230
Gasp!

774
00:35:24,250 --> 00:35:25,060
What?

775
00:35:30,660 --> 00:35:31,300
I'm okay.

776
00:35:31,920 --> 00:35:32,690
I'm fine.

777
00:35:37,090 --> 00:35:37,600
Oh...

778
00:35:37,650 --> 00:35:38,260
Whoa, Mr. Sarm!

779
00:35:38,280 --> 00:35:39,580
- Hey, stupid Sarm!
- Mr. Sarm!

780
00:35:40,580 --> 00:35:41,630
Let's bring him inside.

781
00:35:41,670 --> 00:35:42,640
Okay.

782
00:35:43,090 --> 00:35:44,710
- Mr. Sarm.
- You're so fucking heavy.

783
00:35:45,810 --> 00:35:46,580
Mr. Sarm...

784
00:35:46,600 --> 00:35:49,000
How come my twin brother is this heavy?

785
00:35:51,460 --> 00:35:53,190
Was someone going to give Sarm CPR?

786
00:35:53,350 --> 00:35:54,580
I want to chime in, too!

787
00:35:55,330 --> 00:35:56,620
Sarm!

788
00:36:00,190 --> 00:36:00,740
Uh...

789
00:36:01,320 --> 00:36:02,770
Jam, Ning-nong,

790
00:36:03,190 --> 00:36:04,210
do you two know each other yet?

791
00:36:04,740 --> 00:36:06,250
Did you two happen to meet while working?

792
00:36:07,110 --> 00:36:08,570
Umm, we didn't, actually.

793
00:36:08,860 --> 00:36:11,360
I mostly work at the horse farm

794
00:36:11,380 --> 00:36:13,860
and the pet hospital.

795
00:36:14,020 --> 00:36:15,020
Oh...

796
00:36:15,380 --> 00:36:17,590
Then, you two should get to know each other.

797
00:36:18,270 --> 00:36:18,980
I think...

798
00:36:19,350 --> 00:36:20,800
you're about the same age.

799
00:36:22,150 --> 00:36:23,030
Mm...

800
00:36:24,210 --> 00:36:25,130
I'm Ning-nong.

801
00:36:25,520 --> 00:36:28,880
I'm a vet and the caretaker for Sarm's horses.

802
00:36:30,010 --> 00:36:31,310
I am Jiranat,

803
00:36:32,290 --> 00:36:34,200
Sarm's housekeeper.

804
00:36:41,500 --> 00:36:42,350
Alright...

805
00:36:47,380 --> 00:36:48,790
Just kidding.

806
00:36:49,700 --> 00:36:52,210
I am currently stationed in the engineering department.

807
00:36:52,960 --> 00:36:55,890
Soon, I will probably get rotated over to the horse farm.

808
00:36:56,910 --> 00:36:59,170
Nice to meet you, Doctor Ning-nong.

809
00:37:00,010 --> 00:37:01,990
You can simply call me by my name.

810
00:37:03,350 --> 00:37:05,240
Mm, likewise.

811
00:37:05,270 --> 00:37:06,620
You can just call me by my name.

812
00:37:07,840 --> 00:37:10,090
How long have you been working here?

813
00:37:10,490 --> 00:37:12,320
Only a few months, actually.

814
00:37:12,530 --> 00:37:15,020
Have you had khao soi at the place near the factory?

815
00:37:15,260 --> 00:37:16,270
It is very good.

816
00:37:16,300 --> 00:37:17,490
That sounds tasty, actually.

817
00:37:17,760 --> 00:37:21,360
Do you have any restaurants
or bakeries here that you would recommend?

818
00:37:21,380 --> 00:37:23,210
So I can hurry over and check in.

819
00:37:23,980 --> 00:37:26,180
I actually want to try them all,

820
00:37:26,930 --> 00:37:28,270
but I would need more time

821
00:37:28,770 --> 00:37:31,590
since I am leaving the farm in three months.

822
00:37:34,310 --> 00:37:35,990
Oh, what a shame.

823
00:37:37,290 --> 00:37:39,590
Mm... there are a lot of restaurants around here.

824
00:37:39,710 --> 00:37:42,980
There's a stall by the beer garden,
near the path to the waterfall.

825
00:37:43,180 --> 00:37:44,790
It's my go-to.

826
00:37:45,380 --> 00:37:46,580
I mostly go there...

827
00:37:47,490 --> 00:37:48,780
with Sarm.

828
00:37:48,940 --> 00:37:51,020
Some days, Sarm eats with me.

829
00:37:51,380 --> 00:37:53,780
Other days, he takes me to other restaurants.

830
00:37:54,100 --> 00:37:54,960
But the best one is

831
00:37:54,980 --> 00:37:56,610
the som tam place that serves northeastern Thai food.

832
00:37:57,710 --> 00:37:58,990
But...

833
00:38:00,370 --> 00:38:02,370
can you eat this kind of food?

834
00:38:02,590 --> 00:38:04,460
I can tell just by looking at you

835
00:38:04,700 --> 00:38:06,320
that you're not familiar with them.

836
00:38:10,270 --> 00:38:12,080
I have no problem with any of them.

837
00:38:12,290 --> 00:38:14,410
I am not much of a fan of pla ra, though

838
00:38:14,540 --> 00:38:16,520
But laab with beef blood is at the top of my list.

839
00:38:17,060 --> 00:38:18,960
Suea rong hai, in particular,

840
00:38:18,980 --> 00:38:20,180
is my absolute favorite.

841
00:38:21,240 --> 00:38:22,760
Shall we go there together?

842
00:38:23,020 --> 00:38:24,920
Jam, why not invite Sarm, too?

843
00:38:25,100 --> 00:38:27,150
You should try inviting him, Doctor Ning-nong.

844
00:38:27,180 --> 00:38:28,330
I'd rather not.

845
00:38:28,710 --> 00:38:31,080
I don't know if he's a fan of som tam.

846
00:38:31,550 --> 00:38:33,710
Mr. Sarm is not a picky eater.

847
00:38:34,030 --> 00:38:35,360
He eats all sorts of dishes.

848
00:38:35,480 --> 00:38:36,830
Back on the island,

849
00:38:36,860 --> 00:38:39,000
he went squid fishing with Uncle Keua

850
00:38:39,000 --> 00:38:40,490
and ate it raw.

851
00:38:40,510 --> 00:38:42,620
Occasionally, he would also catch giant grubs

852
00:38:42,980 --> 00:38:45,810
and dip them in salt to eat
while playing cards with Aunt Samrui.

853
00:38:46,980 --> 00:38:47,750
Then...

854
00:38:47,780 --> 00:38:50,180
I guess you should invite him.

855
00:38:50,440 --> 00:38:53,200
Do you usually invite him to places?

856
00:38:53,780 --> 00:38:55,640
I never invite him.

857
00:38:56,180 --> 00:38:58,480
He is the one coming to me.

858
00:39:01,770 --> 00:39:03,080
I did nothing.

859
00:39:03,870 --> 00:39:05,000
He came to me himself.

860
00:39:09,220 --> 00:39:11,430
Why am I even teasing Doctor Ning-nong?

861
00:39:11,950 --> 00:39:12,980
Gosh...

862
00:39:13,470 --> 00:39:14,410
I don't know.

863
00:39:14,910 --> 00:39:16,200
I'm full of jealousy.

864
00:39:22,260 --> 00:39:23,670
Well then, I should get going.

865
00:39:23,690 --> 00:39:25,360
The farm needs me urgently.

866
00:39:25,620 --> 00:39:26,150
Be seeing you.

867
00:39:26,180 --> 00:39:26,590
Oh...

868
00:39:26,730 --> 00:39:28,530
- See you around.
- See you.

869
00:39:31,750 --> 00:39:32,910
By the way, Jam.

870
00:39:33,970 --> 00:39:36,080
Aren't you worried about Sarm?

871
00:39:38,180 --> 00:39:40,380
He has got more than nine lives.

872
00:39:40,740 --> 00:39:42,160
Bad things rarely come his way.

873
00:39:43,470 --> 00:39:45,380
What you said makes sense.

874
00:39:45,740 --> 00:39:47,920
Several years ago, Sarm had a business.

875
00:39:48,040 --> 00:39:49,630
But then he stepped on the local authority's toes,

876
00:39:49,910 --> 00:39:52,820
so he cursed Sarm with black magic.

877
00:39:52,840 --> 00:39:54,280
But Sarm was completely fine.

878
00:39:54,490 --> 00:39:56,030
- Really, Song?
- Yeah.

879
00:39:57,960 --> 00:39:59,780
And Mr. Sarm...

880
00:40:02,310 --> 00:40:03,990
Does he pass out often?

881
00:40:06,450 --> 00:40:07,970
He never passes out, actually.

882
00:40:08,330 --> 00:40:09,760
This came as a surprise to me, too,

883
00:40:09,790 --> 00:40:11,140
seeing him pass out for the first time.

884
00:40:14,780 --> 00:40:15,380
Oh?

885
00:40:16,420 --> 00:40:17,230
What's up?

886
00:40:17,410 --> 00:40:17,780
Mm.

887
00:40:18,040 --> 00:40:18,950
How are you?

888
00:40:23,530 --> 00:40:24,210
Ouch...

889
00:40:25,710 --> 00:40:26,600
I'm a little out of it.

890
00:40:27,270 --> 00:40:28,020
My body feels tired,

891
00:40:28,390 --> 00:40:29,530
like I don't have much energy.

892
00:40:30,860 --> 00:40:31,940
Right, right.

893
00:40:31,960 --> 00:40:33,590
Let me talk to the doctor real quick, okay?

894
00:40:34,580 --> 00:40:35,400
Ow, ow, ow.

895
00:40:35,420 --> 00:40:36,200
Gentle.

896
00:40:45,470 --> 00:40:46,570
Not going to say anything?

897
00:40:49,320 --> 00:40:50,420
Where does it hurt?

898
00:40:50,450 --> 00:40:51,150
Ow.

899
00:40:51,830 --> 00:40:52,390
Ouch...

900
00:40:52,760 --> 00:40:53,540
Right here.

901
00:40:53,570 --> 00:40:54,170
Ow...

902
00:40:54,450 --> 00:40:54,960
It hurts here.

903
00:40:54,980 --> 00:40:55,590
Ow.

904
00:40:55,980 --> 00:40:56,340
Right here.

905
00:40:57,220 --> 00:40:57,770
Here

906
00:40:58,980 --> 00:40:59,970
and right here.

907
00:41:00,220 --> 00:41:01,100
Ouch...

908
00:41:01,950 --> 00:41:03,010
You are

909
00:41:03,380 --> 00:41:04,460
always up late at night,

910
00:41:04,950 --> 00:41:06,980
still working.

911
00:41:07,860 --> 00:41:10,280
Are you going to work 24 hours a day?

912
00:41:11,400 --> 00:41:13,680
You are a human, not a robot.

913
00:41:14,180 --> 00:41:15,580
Know your limits.

914
00:41:16,260 --> 00:41:18,960
Some nights, you are just like that neighbor

915
00:41:18,980 --> 00:41:20,600
who stays up all night doing stuff.

916
00:41:25,080 --> 00:41:25,680
Are you...

917
00:41:26,300 --> 00:41:27,710
even listening to me?

918
00:41:28,470 --> 00:41:29,410
I am.

919
00:41:31,090 --> 00:41:33,630
Well, everything I say goes in one ear and out the other.

920
00:41:35,130 --> 00:41:35,770
Ow...

921
00:41:38,530 --> 00:41:39,380
Feel like I'm going to fall.

922
00:41:39,770 --> 00:41:40,370
Little Jam.

923
00:41:40,580 --> 00:41:41,780
Whoa, whoa. Hey...

924
00:41:43,290 --> 00:41:44,430
Why do you not sit down first?

925
00:41:45,060 --> 00:41:46,570
I will go get the doctor for you.

926
00:41:48,980 --> 00:41:50,180
No need, Little Jam.

927
00:41:50,530 --> 00:41:51,770
No need for the doctor.

928
00:41:52,910 --> 00:41:54,190
Hugging you

929
00:41:56,180 --> 00:41:57,380
right here

930
00:41:57,960 --> 00:41:59,400
is enough to recharge my energy.

931
00:42:00,690 --> 00:42:02,160
Soon, I'll be back on my feet

932
00:42:02,180 --> 00:42:03,380
and stronger than ever.

933
00:42:12,050 --> 00:42:12,980
Little Jam.

934
00:42:14,360 --> 00:42:14,930
Hm?

935
00:42:21,810 --> 00:42:23,060
The truth is, I...

936
00:42:25,630 --> 00:42:26,460
I...

937
00:42:27,720 --> 00:42:30,980
You are going to make a joke about
being the president of the company, right?

938
00:42:31,430 --> 00:42:32,600
Listen, Little Jam.

939
00:42:33,350 --> 00:42:34,550
I'm being serious.

940
00:42:34,910 --> 00:42:35,950
I'm dead serious.

941
00:42:36,340 --> 00:42:37,390
I really am.

942
00:42:38,670 --> 00:42:40,390
Listen carefully, okay?

943
00:42:42,180 --> 00:42:42,800
Mm.

944
00:42:44,580 --> 00:42:45,380
I...

945
00:42:47,780 --> 00:42:48,610
I...

946
00:42:55,100 --> 00:42:55,800
I...

947
00:43:03,060 --> 00:43:03,620
I...

948
00:43:06,710 --> 00:43:07,420
I...

949
00:43:09,730 --> 00:43:10,170
I...

950
00:43:10,200 --> 00:43:11,010
- Sarm.
- love...

951
00:43:13,600 --> 00:43:14,400
Why are you here?

952
00:43:14,430 --> 00:43:15,950
I didn't even summon you here.

953
00:43:16,110 --> 00:43:16,890
What the hell?

954
00:43:16,930 --> 00:43:18,860
Watch that foul mouth of yours, Sarm.

955
00:43:18,950 --> 00:43:20,500
I'm here for Jam.

956
00:43:20,530 --> 00:43:22,270
I've had him booked since 1:30 P.M.

957
00:43:22,490 --> 00:43:25,020
We're having shabu-shabu at the back of the farm.

958
00:43:25,420 --> 00:43:26,530
What about you?

959
00:43:27,090 --> 00:43:28,140
Why are you still here?

960
00:43:28,460 --> 00:43:29,580
Why don't you go home already?

961
00:43:44,990 --> 00:43:46,600
My twin brother

962
00:43:47,420 --> 00:43:49,140
is clearly falling in love.

963
00:43:49,610 --> 00:43:51,380
I just don't know who it is.

964
00:43:51,670 --> 00:43:52,580
Ning-nong?

965
00:43:53,630 --> 00:43:54,440
Or is it...

966
00:43:55,850 --> 00:43:57,100
Lantao?

967
00:43:58,740 --> 00:44:00,610
He takes good care of so many people

968
00:44:00,820 --> 00:44:02,180
that I feel like he belongs to everyone.

969
00:44:04,140 --> 00:44:05,110
If I want to find out,

970
00:44:05,410 --> 00:44:06,710
I'll have to find the answer myself.

971
00:44:08,310 --> 00:44:09,620
Curse you, Sarm.

972
00:44:19,430 --> 00:44:20,180
Shit!

973
00:44:20,680 --> 00:44:22,010
He has Jam with him!

974
00:44:22,030 --> 00:44:23,030
Sarm!

975
00:44:25,480 --> 00:44:26,610
Damn it, Sarm...

976
00:44:27,310 --> 00:44:29,100
You're going for the golden boy?

977
00:44:50,780 --> 00:44:52,580
Hello, Mr. Thee.

978
00:44:54,280 --> 00:44:55,470
We've met before.

979
00:44:57,850 --> 00:45:00,480
There is still a lot more that I need to learn.

980
00:45:01,420 --> 00:45:03,220
Please take care of me and guide me.

981
00:45:05,690 --> 00:45:07,610
"Mr. Thee" sounds a bit too distant.

982
00:45:08,300 --> 00:45:10,190
You can call me by my name.

983
00:45:10,710 --> 00:45:12,210
It sounds far more pleasing.

984
00:45:14,300 --> 00:45:15,620
If so...

985
00:45:17,170 --> 00:45:18,980
allow me to call you by your name.

986
00:45:20,440 --> 00:45:21,380
With pleasure.

987
00:45:23,500 --> 00:45:24,970
By the way, Jam...

988
00:45:25,470 --> 00:45:26,450
You owe me one.

989
00:45:28,240 --> 00:45:30,170
Since when have I owed you?

990
00:45:31,450 --> 00:45:33,880
You owe me a thank-you.

991
00:45:35,490 --> 00:45:36,250
Well...

992
00:45:36,510 --> 00:45:38,470
I want you to repay me by...

993
00:45:39,570 --> 00:45:42,190
having lunch with me every day,

994
00:45:42,460 --> 00:45:43,410
and with no one else.

995
00:45:51,610 --> 00:45:52,310
Right.

996
00:46:03,050 --> 00:46:04,100
Bye.

997
00:46:13,890 --> 00:46:14,590
Jam!

998
00:46:17,470 --> 00:46:18,980
Lantao, how did you get here?

999
00:46:19,340 --> 00:46:21,640
I'm here to find the love of my life.

1000
00:46:22,740 --> 00:46:24,090
You work here?

1001
00:46:24,410 --> 00:46:25,480
That's right.

1002
00:46:25,580 --> 00:46:27,200
I work in the QC department.

1003
00:46:27,380 --> 00:46:29,020
No, and it's not 'cause Sarm pulled some strings.

1004
00:46:29,160 --> 00:46:29,790
Yesterday,

1005
00:46:29,810 --> 00:46:32,180
Sarm himself told me to apply for a job here.

1006
00:46:32,490 --> 00:46:35,100
And I got the job on my own merits.

1007
00:46:37,220 --> 00:46:38,010
By the way,

1008
00:46:38,150 --> 00:46:39,830
you work here, too, Jam?

1009
00:46:39,910 --> 00:46:40,400
Mm.

1010
00:46:41,230 --> 00:46:42,590
But I will not be here for long.

1011
00:46:42,820 --> 00:46:44,500
I am only here short-term.

1012
00:46:44,810 --> 00:46:45,380
Oh.

1013
00:46:45,400 --> 00:46:46,940
And where are you staying?

1014
00:46:48,020 --> 00:46:50,180
I am staying in the quarters in the Replica Town Zone.

1015
00:46:50,810 --> 00:46:52,980
Are you in a hurry to get home this evening?

1016
00:46:56,590 --> 00:46:58,010
Are you inviting me to go somewhere?

1017
00:46:58,470 --> 00:46:59,610
To have Thai BBQ.

1018
00:47:00,560 --> 00:47:01,280
Mm.

1019
00:47:01,860 --> 00:47:02,440
I am down.

1020
00:47:05,030 --> 00:47:05,550
Yay!

1021
00:47:06,310 --> 00:47:07,120
Jam,

1022
00:47:07,460 --> 00:47:08,920
let's make the most of tonight.

1023
00:47:09,980 --> 00:47:10,790
Sorry,

1024
00:47:10,800 --> 00:47:12,340
all the tables are taken.

1025
00:47:13,390 --> 00:47:14,020
What about that one?

1026
00:47:14,040 --> 00:47:15,860
It's already reserved.

1027
00:47:18,060 --> 00:47:19,180
Jam...

1028
00:47:19,870 --> 00:47:21,080
Do you want to sit with me?

1029
00:47:21,480 --> 00:47:22,350
Apparently,

1030
00:47:22,380 --> 00:47:23,640
my friends ditched me.

1031
00:47:26,180 --> 00:47:28,110
Are we bothering you, Wasin?

1032
00:47:41,220 --> 00:47:42,790
I just want to find Sarm.

1033
00:47:43,750 --> 00:47:45,910
So why does the farm have to be this vast?

1034
00:47:47,420 --> 00:47:48,080
Ow.

1035
00:47:48,480 --> 00:47:49,240
Oh...

1036
00:47:59,120 --> 00:48:00,410
Are you alright?

1037
00:48:02,030 --> 00:48:04,220
I'm gonna go look for the love of my life.

1038
00:48:04,770 --> 00:48:06,390
And my legs hurt.

1039
00:48:07,060 --> 00:48:07,720
Come here.

1040
00:48:07,750 --> 00:48:08,180
Ow.

1041
00:48:10,940 --> 00:48:13,000
Why did you slip out of the medical center?

1042
00:48:13,450 --> 00:48:14,430
How did you know?

1043
00:48:15,220 --> 00:48:16,330
It's the gown.

1044
00:48:20,610 --> 00:48:21,780
I didn't.

1045
00:48:22,060 --> 00:48:23,620
I just didn't tell anyone I'd left.

1046
00:48:24,980 --> 00:48:26,820
I don't want to be there anymore.

1047
00:48:27,150 --> 00:48:28,220
Why not?

1048
00:48:28,390 --> 00:48:29,550
Were the doctors being strict?

1049
00:48:30,070 --> 00:48:31,330
Sarm wasn't there.

1050
00:48:31,940 --> 00:48:33,630
Do you know where he is?

1051
00:48:34,950 --> 00:48:36,070
I don't really know.

1052
00:48:36,090 --> 00:48:37,500
It's just Wasin here,

1053
00:48:37,740 --> 00:48:40,100
and he's taking you back to the medical center.

1054
00:48:40,690 --> 00:48:41,180
Come.

1055
00:48:41,280 --> 00:48:41,860
Come on.

1056
00:48:41,880 --> 00:48:42,920
I'm not going with you.

1057
00:48:43,450 --> 00:48:45,270
I'm gonna go look for the love of my life.

1058
00:48:45,300 --> 00:48:46,500
Your legs are still hurting.

1059
00:48:47,040 --> 00:48:48,480
The doctors will be looking all over for you again.

1060
00:48:48,510 --> 00:48:49,610
I'm not going!

1061
00:48:50,280 --> 00:48:51,290
Oh...

1062
00:48:51,380 --> 00:48:52,840
Should've stayed away.

1063
00:48:53,010 --> 00:48:54,460
And now I've been scratched by a cat.

1064
00:48:54,590 --> 00:48:55,970
Why did you grab me, then?

1065
00:48:56,150 --> 00:48:57,350
You're a stubborn cat,

1066
00:48:57,380 --> 00:48:58,910
so into the basket you go.

1067
00:49:01,640 --> 00:49:02,590
Not at all.

1068
00:49:02,620 --> 00:49:03,920
Sitting here by myself

1069
00:49:03,950 --> 00:49:04,580
is kind of lonely.

1070
00:49:05,900 --> 00:49:06,470
Come on.

1071
00:49:06,750 --> 00:49:07,310
Well, then...

1072
00:49:07,330 --> 00:49:09,010
- We will join you.
- The seats are yours.

1073
00:49:09,380 --> 00:49:09,980
Come on.

1074
00:49:13,160 --> 00:49:13,850
Excuse me,

1075
00:49:14,030 --> 00:49:16,070
could we get some extra sets of dishes?

1076
00:49:16,150 --> 00:49:17,210
Make it two.

1077
00:49:31,500 --> 00:49:32,360
Thank you.

1078
00:49:32,440 --> 00:49:33,610
These are yours.

1079
00:49:47,350 --> 00:49:49,290
Well, well, Lantao.

1080
00:49:49,340 --> 00:49:50,680
Looking at me like that,

1081
00:49:51,030 --> 00:49:52,860
do you have a problem with me?

1082
00:49:53,970 --> 00:49:54,960
If you weren't looking at me,

1083
00:49:55,920 --> 00:49:57,690
how did you know I was?

1084
00:49:58,530 --> 00:49:59,980
Because I was looking at you.

1085
00:50:00,780 --> 00:50:01,950
Why, though?

1086
00:50:02,180 --> 00:50:03,180
Um...

1087
00:50:04,120 --> 00:50:05,180
Because you're cute, I guess?

1088
00:50:05,880 --> 00:50:08,020
Quit being a player, Wasin.

1089
00:50:08,340 --> 00:50:09,850
I hate players!

1090
00:50:10,730 --> 00:50:12,350
I'm no player.

1091
00:50:12,660 --> 00:50:13,870
I'm just looking at you.

1092
00:50:14,180 --> 00:50:15,080
Ew...

1093
00:50:15,770 --> 00:50:17,530
Don't mess with me.

1094
00:50:18,070 --> 00:50:19,700
I like Sarm,

1095
00:50:20,070 --> 00:50:21,580
and no one else.

1096
00:50:22,670 --> 00:50:24,190
Why do you like Mr. Sarm?

1097
00:50:26,390 --> 00:50:27,850
Cause he's handsome.

1098
00:50:29,320 --> 00:50:31,570
I like someone who's good-looking and caring.

1099
00:50:32,180 --> 00:50:34,030
A caring person?

1100
00:50:34,820 --> 00:50:36,920
What about someone who wears a helmet?

1101
00:50:39,080 --> 00:50:39,780
Hm?

1102
00:50:40,050 --> 00:50:41,140
I don't want one.

1103
00:50:42,100 --> 00:50:43,570
I don't like engineers.

1104
00:50:44,860 --> 00:50:46,580
Be careful what you hate,

1105
00:50:46,990 --> 00:50:48,500
because you might end up with one.

1106
00:50:50,500 --> 00:50:51,900
Wasin, you're talking nonsense.

1107
00:50:59,530 --> 00:50:59,990
Here.

1108
00:51:04,360 --> 00:51:04,860
Here.

1109
00:51:05,060 --> 00:51:06,630
This one's yours, Jam.

1110
00:51:08,070 --> 00:51:10,110
Why did you give this to me?

1111
00:51:10,310 --> 00:51:11,610
I already have one on my plate.

1112
00:51:12,140 --> 00:51:12,960
Here.

1113
00:51:12,980 --> 00:51:13,960
You're exhausted, Jam.

1114
00:51:13,980 --> 00:51:15,300
You've been working all day,

1115
00:51:16,490 --> 00:51:18,050
so you need to eat well.

1116
00:51:40,970 --> 00:51:41,780
What's wrong?

1117
00:51:44,240 --> 00:51:45,360
No, you.

1118
00:51:45,380 --> 00:51:46,410
What are you doing here?

1119
00:51:47,240 --> 00:51:48,110
I'm here to pick you up.

1120
00:51:59,400 --> 00:52:00,260
What is it?

1121
00:52:02,350 --> 00:52:03,170
Are you awake?

1122
00:52:07,220 --> 00:52:07,970
Gosh...

1123
00:52:11,500 --> 00:52:12,930
Make sure you're free this evening.

1124
00:52:13,400 --> 00:52:14,480
I am already occupied.

1125
00:52:23,880 --> 00:52:24,610
With who?

1126
00:52:24,710 --> 00:52:25,330
And where?

1127
00:52:27,380 --> 00:52:29,380
Thee invited me to a green market.

1128
00:52:36,060 --> 00:52:36,810
You two are close?

1129
00:52:38,180 --> 00:52:39,780
And I cannot be?

1130
00:52:42,980 --> 00:52:43,730
No.

1131
00:52:44,820 --> 00:52:45,700
Nothing.

1132
00:52:46,550 --> 00:52:47,390
I won't let you go.

1133
00:52:51,750 --> 00:52:52,960
Who are you

1134
00:52:52,990 --> 00:52:54,830
to stop me from going wherever I want?

1135
00:52:56,590 --> 00:52:57,210
I don't care.

1136
00:52:57,710 --> 00:52:58,500
I won't let you go.

1137
00:52:58,530 --> 00:52:59,760
Meet me in the evening.

1138
00:52:59,950 --> 00:53:01,550
I've got something for you to do until late.

1139
00:53:03,860 --> 00:53:06,630
Evenings are after work hours.

1140
00:53:07,030 --> 00:53:09,320
I can report this to the Ministry of Labour.

1141
00:53:29,160 --> 00:53:30,260
Come stand right here, Jam.

1142
